E["npc:jaina-proudmoore"] = {t="npc",n="Jaina Proudmoore",z="dustwallow",s="Lady Jaina Proudmoore is the ruler of Theramore Isle and the most powerful human sorceress alive. Formerly a star pupil of Dalaran's Kirin Tor, she led the survivors of Lordaeron across the Great Sea and now strives to maintain a fragile peace between the Alliance and the New Horde.",h="Lady Jaina Proudmoore is the ruler of Theramore Isle and the most powerful human sorceress alive.",sec={{t="Flight to Kalimdor",b="The daughter of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras, Jaina showed remarkable aptitude for the arcane at an early age and studied under Archmage Antonidas in Dalaran. During the Third War, she investigated the mysterious Plague of Undeath alongside Prince Arthas Menethil, witnessing firsthand the tragic downfall of Lordaeron. Guided by the warnings of the Prophet Medivh, she rallied an expedition of human survivors and set sail westward to the forgotten continent of Kalimdor. There, her forces forged an unprecedented alliance with Thrall's Horde and the night elves, standing together atop Mount Hyjal to defeat Archimonde and shatter the Burning Legion's invasion.",sp=0},{t="The Lady of Theramore",b="Following the Legion's defeat, Jaina founded the island citadel of Theramore off the coast of Dustwallow Marsh, establishing the primary bastion of the Alliance in southern Kalimdor. Her commitment to diplomacy was tested to its limits when her father arrived seeking vengeance against the orcs; Jaina refused to support his war, stepping aside as Thrall's forces slew the Grand Admiral to prevent Kalimdor from plunging into another devastating conflict. Today, she rules Theramore as a steadfast advocate for coexistence, working closely with Warchief Thrall while anchoring the Alliance's presence against rising local tensions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lady Jaina Proudmoore?",a="Jaina is the ruler of Theramore Isle and arguably the most gifted human mage alive. She is the daughter of the late Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras and a former apprentice of Archmage Antonidas in Dalaran.",al={"who is jaina","jaina proudmoore lore","theramore leader"}},{q="Why is Jaina in Kalimdor instead of the Eastern Kingdoms?",a="Before the fall of Lordaeron in the Third War, the Prophet Medivh warned Jaina to lead as many people as possible across the sea to Kalimdor. Her expedition survived the journey, fought at Mount Hyjal, and settled the port-fortress of Theramore in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"why did jaina leave lordaeron","jaina kalimdor","why is theramore here"}},{q="What is Jaina's relationship with the Horde?",a="Jaina maintains an unusual, cautious friendship with Warchief Thrall. After fighting together against the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal, both leaders have strived to keep the peace between their peoples, despite sharp opposition from hardliners on both sides.",al={"is jaina friendly with thrall","jaina and horde","does jaina hate orcs"}},{q="What happened between Jaina and Prince Arthas Menethil?",a="Jaina and Arthas were childhood friends whose bond deepened into romance as young adults. They jointly investigated the plague spreading across Lordaeron, but Jaina was horrified by Arthas's descent into ruthlessness—culminating in the purging of Stratholme, where she refused to participate in the slaughter of infected citizens.",al={"jaina and arthas","did jaina love arthas"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Trained under Archmage Antonidas himself, Lady Jaina is widely considered the most powerful living human sorceress, demonstrating the height of Dalaran's arcane mastery.",["faction:Alliance"]="Jaina provides the Alliance with its critical foothold in southern Kalimdor, balancing loyalty to Highlord Bolvar's regency in Stormwind against her desire to avoid war with the neighboring Horde."},kw={"antonidas","arthas","dustwallow","jaina","kirin tor","proudmoore","theramore","thrall"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:dalaran","topic:new-horde","topic:burning-legion","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:medivh","topic:kul-tiras","topic:third-war"},src={"Jaina Proudmoore"}}
E["npc:overlord-mok-morokk"] = {t="npc",n="Overlord Mok'Morokk",z="dustwallow",s="Overlord Mok'Morokk is the brute chieftain of the Stonemaul ogres, presiding over Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow Marsh. Originally appointed by Rexxar for his strength, he has become a tyrannical and cowardly ruler who refuses to defend his clan against the black dragonflight.",h="Overlord Mok'Morokk is the brute chieftain of the Stonemaul ogres, presiding over Brackenwall Village in...",sec={{t="A Tyrant in the Marsh",b="When Rexxar bested the previous chieftain Kor'gall and led the Stonemaul clan in defense of Durotar, he left Mok'Morokk in command, seeing promise in his sheer martial strength. That faith proved misplaced. Mok'Morokk quickly succumbed to the corrupting influence of absolute authority, ruling through intimidation and self-indulgence rather than stewardship. Instead of caring for his kin, he demands unearned tribute, lounges in Brackenwall Village, and bullies anyone who questions his command.",sp=0},{t="The Coward of Brackenwall",b="Mok'Morokk's leadership crumbled entirely when the black dragonflight descended upon the ancestral Stonemaul Village, slaying many ogres and driving the survivors into the muck of Brackenwall. Rather than rallying a counterattack to reclaim their home or avenge the dead, Mok'Morokk forbade any action, cowering from the dragons' wrath. Discontent festers among his advisers, such as the ogre mage Draz'Zilb, who quietly seek outside champions willing to challenge the overlord's shameful reign.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Overlord Mok'Morokk?",a="Mok'Morokk is the chieftain of the Stonemaul ogres, currently residing in Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow Marsh. He was named leader by Rexxar but quickly degenerated into a selfish and demanding despot.",al={"who is mok'morokk","brackenwall leader","stonemaul ogre boss"}},{q="How did Mok'Morokk become leader of the Stonemaul clan?",a="During the founding of Durotar, the Champion of the Horde, Rexxar, defeated the clan's previous leader and took command of the Stonemaul. When Rexxar departed to wander the wilderness, he appointed Mok'Morokk as overlord because of his raw physical strength.",al={"how did mok'morokk get in charge","rexxar chose mok'morokk","why is he chieftain"}},{q="Why are the Stonemaul ogres in Brackenwall Village?",a="The Stonemaul ogres originally lived in Stonemaul Village, but black dragons attacked and razed their settlement. The survivors fled north into the swamps to establish Brackenwall Village as a refugee outpost.",al={"why did ogres move to brackenwall","what happened to stonemaul village","black dragon attack ogres"}},{q="Why won't Mok'Morokk fight the black dragonflight?",a="Despite his massive size and fierce reputation, Mok'Morokk is terrified of the dragons. Rather than leading a counterattack to reclaim his clan's ancestral territory, he sits idle in Brackenwall, hoarding tribute and ignoring the cries of his people.",al={"why doesn't mok'morokk fight dragons","is mok'morokk a coward","retake stonemaul"}},{q="Do the other Stonemaul ogres respect Mok'Morokk?",a="The clan grows increasingly resentful of his laziness, cowardice, and bullying. His advisers worry about the future of the Stonemaul under his rule.",al={"do ogres like mok'morokk","draz'zilb mok'morokk","stonemaul rebellion"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Stonemaul ogres are valuable allies sworn to the Horde since Rexxar's campaign, but Mok'Morokk's ineffective and cowardly leadership threatens to leave Brackenwall Village completely vulnerable.",["class:Warrior"]="Mok'Morokk is a textbook example of raw martial strength unguided by honor or courage, demonstrating how easily brute force degenerates into cowardice and tyranny."},kw={"brackenwall","draz'zilb","dustwallow","mok'morokk","ogre","overlord","rexxar","stonemaul"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow","topic:black-dragonflight","topic:horde","zone:durotar","npc:onyxia"},src={"Overlord Mok'Morokk"}}
E["npc:tabetha"] = {t="npc",n="Tabetha",z="dustwallow",s="Tabetha is a reclusive, powerful human mage dwelling deep within Dustwallow Marsh at an isolated farmstead in the Quagmire. Far from the politics of Dalaran or Theramore, she instructs aspiring spellcasters and aids those seeking mastery over potent arcane and occult relics.",h="Tabetha is a reclusive, powerful human mage dwelling deep within Dustwallow Marsh at an isolated farmstead in...",sec={{t="Hermit of the Quagmire",b="Hidden away in the sodden expanse of Dustwallow Marsh north of the Stonemaul Ruins, Tabetha lives in a secluded shack alongside her apprentices. Surrounding herself with alchemical vials and ancient tomes, she has deliberately chosen solitude over the academic hierarchies of the Eastern Kingdoms. Despite her remote location, her mastery of the arcane is renowned enough that spellcasters across Kalimdor brave beasts and mire alike to seek her guidance.",sp=0},{t="A Neutral Mentor",b="Tabetha stands notably apart from factional hostilities. While human by birth, she turns away neither Alliance nor Horde initiates who demonstrate the will to learn, providing tutelage to mages and assisting warlocks with dangerous bindings such as the Orb of Orahil. Her past connects her to figures like Menara Voidrender, revealing an extensive history with esoteric magic that transcends simple faction allegiance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Tabetha?",a="Tabetha lives in a secluded shack at Tabetha's Farm, situated deep within the Quagmire in western Dustwallow Marsh, just north of the Stonemaul Ruins.",al={"tabetha location","where is tabetha","tabetha farm map"}},{q="Is Tabetha hostile to Horde players?",a="No. Despite being human, Tabetha is neutral. She teaches apprentices and aids spellcasters of both the Horde and the Alliance without discrimination.",al={"is tabetha alliance only","can horde talk to tabetha","tabetha faction"}},{q="Why do mages and warlocks seek her out?",a="Tabetha possesses rare knowledge regarding arcane rituals, magical foci, and binding rites. Mages consult her for craft mastery and power trials, while warlocks seek her expertise to cleanse or bind potent artifacts like the Orb of Orahil.",al={"why visit tabetha","tabetha class quest","orb of orahil tabetha"}},{q="What is her connection to Menara Voidrender?",a="Tabetha shares an established history with Menara Voidrender. While their paths have diverged, their mutual understanding of powerful relics and binding magic links them across their respective hermitages.",al={"tabetha and menara","menara voidrender history"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Tabetha is an essential mentor for mid-level mages, testing your grasp of arcane rituals and sending you across dangerous lands like Uldaman to refine your craft.",["class:Warlock"]="Though she practices the arcane, Tabetha's deep understanding of magical relics makes her a critical guide when dealing with dangerous artifacts like the Infernal Orb and the Orb of Orahil."},kw={"dustwallow marsh","mage quest","menara voidrender","orb of orahil","quagmire","tabetha","tabetha's farm"},rel={"subzone:tabetha-s-farm","zone:dustwallow","subzone:quagmire","npc:menara-voidrender","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","subzone:uldaman"},src={"Tabetha"}}
E["quest:1132"] = {t="quest",n="Fiora Longears",z="dustwallow",s="This errand introduces Alliance adventurers from the Eastern Kingdoms to the untamed continent of Kalimdor. Directed by the enthusiastic recruiter Red Jack Flint in Menethil Harbor, travelers take ship across the Great Sea to report to his high elf contact, Fiora Longears, in the inn of Theramore.",h="This errand introduces Alliance adventurers from the Eastern Kingdoms to the untamed continent of Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Call to the West",b="For many humans, dwarves, and gnomes, the Eastern Kingdoms feel fraught with old conflicts and scarred earth. In the bustling port of Menethil Harbor, the sailor Red Jack Flint spends his days urging adventurous travelers to board a vessel bound across the Great Sea. Describing Kalimdor as an uncharted realm of fortune and opportunity, Flint directs bold wanderers to Theramore to meet his associate, an elf named Fiora Longears.",sp=0},{t="Arrival in Theramore",b="Crossing the ocean brings travelers to Theramore, an Alliance port on the coast of Dustwallow Marsh. Waiting in the town inn, Fiora Longears receives arrivals recommended by Flint. Trusting Flint's eye for character, Fiora welcomes newly arrived Alliance heroes and prepares to direct them inland toward the ancient forests of Ashenvale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fiora Longears?",a="Fiora Longears is a high elf stationed in the inn of Theramore in Dustwallow Marsh. She acts as a welcoming partner and contact for Red Jack Flint, greeting Alliance travelers arriving from the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"fiora longears","who is fiora"},it="identity"},{q="Who starts this quest?",a="The quest is offered by Red Jack Flint, an energetic human sailor located in Menethil Harbor along the coast of the Wetlands.",al={"quest giver","where to get fiora longears quest","who gives quest"},gp=true},{q="How do I reach Fiora Longears from Menethil Harbor?",a="Board the passenger vessel docked at Menethil Harbor that sails westward across the Great Sea directly to Theramore in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"how to get to theramore","ship to theramore","boat from menethil"},gp=true},{q="What happens after meeting Fiora Longears?",a="Upon greeting you in Theramore, Fiora commends Flint's recommendation and offers the next leg of your journey, sending you inland to Astranaar in Ashenvale.",al={"what comes next","follow up quest","journey to astranaar quest"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the relationship between Red Jack Flint and Fiora Longears?",a="Flint refers to Fiora as his partner across the sea. While Flint scouts eager adventurers in the Eastern Kingdoms, Fiora receives them in Kalimdor to facilitate Alliance operations and travel inland.",al={"are flint and fiora partners","red jack flint fiora connection"},it="ties"},{q="Why is the Alliance recruiting travelers to Kalimdor?",a="Kalimdor represents vast new territory and resources for the Alliance, as well as a front where night elven allies need assistance protecting their ancestral lands from threats like the Horde and demonic remnants.",al={"why go to kalimdor","why theramore"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Red Jack Flint want to send you to Kalimdor?",a="Red Jack Flint sees himself as an agent of opportunity, tasked with inspiring promising adventurers in Menethil Harbor to cross the Great Sea. Bound to the docks himself and longing for ocean voyages, his role is to spot hardy souls and direct them to his high elf partner, Fiora Longears, who helps newcomers find their footing and take up the Alliance's burgeoning efforts across Kalimdor.",al={"red jack flint motive","why send me to fiora","why does jack flint want this done"},it="motive",add="869cd7aa"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This journey represents the bridge between the Eastern Kingdoms and the night elven territories of Kalimdor, uniting the Alliance's eastern and western frontiers.",["race:NightElf"]="Fiora Longears serves as an official welcoming presence for eastern allies arriving at Theramore, preparing them for the ancient wilds of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"theramore","boat","dustwallow marsh","fiora longears","kalimdor","menethil harbor","red jack flint","wetlands"},rel={"npc:red-jack-flint","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:dustwallow","quest:1133","subzone:astranaar"},m={start="Red Jack Flint",["end"]="Fiora Longears",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1132},src={"Fiora Longears (quest)"}}
E["subzone:beezil-s-wreck"] = {t="subzone",n="Beezil's Wreck",z="dustwallow",s="Beezil's Wreck marks the crash site of an unfortunate goblin zeppelin deep within the quagmires of Dustwallow Marsh. Resting east of Tabetha's Farm, the shattered vessel's cargo holds scattered supplies and volatile engineering components that attract scavengers.",h="Beezil's Wreck marks the crash site of an unfortunate goblin zeppelin deep within the quagmires of Dustwallow...",sec={{t="A Calamitous Landing",b="Hidden away in the humid muck east of Tabetha's Farm lies the splintered skeleton of a goblin zeppelin known as Beezil's Wreck. The craft was hauling cargo southward across Kalimdor before suffering a disastrous plunge into the swamp. While the wreckage still smolders amid tangled reeds, its eccentric captain, Beezil, has seemingly vanished from the marsh, leaving behind scattered crates and ticking machinery to slowly rot in the brine.",sp=0},{t="Salvage in the Muck",b="Despite the harsh environment, the crash site remains a prime target for opportunistic explorers. The airship carried a payload of volatile goods, notably Seaforium boosters and heavy crates that survived the impact. Scavengers daring enough to wade through the surrounding beasts often risk life and limb to secure what is left of the lost shipment before corrosive marsh water ruins the haul entirely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Beezil's Wreck?",a="Beezil's Wreck is the crash site of a goblin zeppelin situated deep in Dustwallow Marsh, directly east of Tabetha's Farm. The airship came down while transporting cargo across the marsh.",al={"beezils wreck","crashed zeppelin dustwallow","what is this wreck"}},{q="Where is the pilot, Beezil?",a="The pilot, Beezil, is nowhere to be found around the crash site. Whether he escaped into the treacherous wilderness or fled the marsh entirely remains a mystery to those searching the hull.",al={"where is beezil","who is beezil","beezil location"}},{q="What valuable cargo was the zeppelin carrying?",a="The zeppelin was loaded with trade goods and volatile goblin technology, including Seaforium boosters. These valuable engineering components make the site a frequent target for adventurers and salvagers.",al={"what was in the zeppelin","seaforium boosters","wreck cargo"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The twisted wreckage of a goblin zeppelin holds volatile mechanical components, particularly Seaforium boosters that any tinkerer would covet.",["race:Gnome"]="Examining the smoking remains of rival goblin aviation offers a morbid reminder of the perils inherent in non-gnomish aerial design."},kw={"beezil","beezil's wreck","dustwallow marsh","seaforium","tabetha","zeppelin crash"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:tabetha-s-farm","npc:tabetha","topic:goblin"},src={"Beezil's Wreck"}}
E["subzone:bloodfen-burrow"] = {t="subzone",n="Bloodfen Burrow",z="dustwallow",s="Bloodfen Burrow is a cavern in southwestern Dustwallow Marsh swarming with vicious raptors. The beasts have claimed the cave and the surrounding clearing, completely overrunning the ruins of a settlement that once tried to survive the wetlands.",h="Bloodfen Burrow is a cavern in southwestern Dustwallow Marsh swarming with vicious raptors.",sec={{t="A Den of Predators",b="Tucked away in the southwestern reaches of Dustwallow Marsh, Bloodfen Burrow serves as the primary den for the region's aggressive Bloodfen raptors. The cave mouth and surrounding hollow crawl with the pack, drawn to the sheltered crevice and the bountiful hunting ground the marsh provides. Just outside the entrance lie scattered debris and splintered remains of an unidentified settlement, serving as a grim reminder of who truly rules the swamp's interior. Travelers also whisper that Cortello, an adventurous buccaneer, left one of his hidden riddle clues somewhere within this deadly den.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What lives in Bloodfen Burrow?",a="The burrow is overrun by Bloodfen raptors. They have established a dense nesting ground both inside the cave and across the surrounding clearing, attacking anyone foolish enough to intrude on their territory.",al={"who lives here","bloodfen burrow raptors","what mobs in bloodfen burrow"}},{q="What are the ruins outside the cave?",a="The remains of an unidentified settlement lie outside the cave. Raptors destroyed the settlement, but the identity and fate of its occupants are not recorded.",al={"ruined settlement dustwallow","who built the huts near bloodfen burrow","ruins outside cave"}},{q="Why would an adventurer search Bloodfen Burrow?",a="Aside from hunting the fierce marsh raptors, explorers deciphering Cortello's Riddle must venture inside the burrow. The pirate left one of his riddle clues concealed within the cavern's shadowy depths.",al={"cortello's riddle bloodfen","treasure in bloodfen burrow","bloodfen burrow quest"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The Bloodfen raptors nesting here are fierce, quick beasts well-suited for hunters seeking durable, aggressive swamp companions."},kw={"bloodfen burrow","bloodfen raptor","cortello's riddle","dustwallow marsh","raptor cave"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},src={"Bloodfen Burrow"}}
E["subzone:bluefen"] = {t="subzone",n="Bluefen",z="dustwallow",s="Bluefen is a soggy marshland nestled in northern Dustwallow Marsh between Brackenwall Village and Blackhoof Village. Crawling with aggressive wetland predators, the mire has also become a staging ground for covert Theramore Infiltrators keeping watch on local Horde movements.",h="Bluefen is a soggy marshland nestled in northern Dustwallow Marsh between Brackenwall Village and Blackhoof...",sec={{t="A Contested Bog",b="Situated between the Stonemaul ogres of Brackenwall Village to the west and the grimtotem tauren of Blackhoof Village to the east, Bluefen embodies the untamed hazards of Dustwallow Marsh. The humid swampland teems with predatory beasts, including raptors, giant spiders, carrion-feeding birds, and lurking crocolisks. Beyond natural predators, travelers must contend with Theramore Infiltrators who skulk through the murky terrain to spy on the Horde and project human influence deeper into the swamp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Bluefen located?",a="Bluefen lies in northern Dustwallow Marsh, situated directly between Brackenwall Village to the west and Blackhoof Village to the east.",al={"bluefen location","where is bluefen","bluefen map"}},{q="What threats can be found in Bluefen?",a="The marsh is infested with dangerous wildlife including spiders, crocolisks, raptors, and marsh birds. Additionally, covert Theramore Infiltrators scout the area, posing a threat to Horde travelers.",al={"bluefen enemies","what lives in bluefen","bluefen mobs"}},{q="Why are Theramore scouts active in Bluefen?",a="Theramore Infiltrators monitor northern Dustwallow Marsh from Bluefen, watching the neighboring Stonemaul ogre settlement of Brackenwall Village and patrolling the contested pathways of the marsh.",al={"theramore infiltrators","why are alliance here","theramore spies"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Positioned just east of Brackenwall Village, Bluefen poses a double danger to Horde champions: fierce swamp beasts and watchful Theramore Infiltrators spying on your Stonemaul allies.",["faction:Alliance"]="While wild beasts make travel treacherous, Theramore scouts use the dense marshland foliage of Bluefen to keep watchful eyes on nearby ogre and tauren encampments."},kw={"blackhoof","bluefen","brackenwall","crocolisks","dustwallow","marsh","theramore infiltrators"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:brackenwall-village"},src={"Bluefen"}}
E["subzone:brackenwall-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Brackenwall Village",z="dustwallow",s="Brackenwall Village is the primary Horde outpost in Dustwallow Marsh, nestled among the bogs in the northwest corner of the zone. Founded by surviving Stonemaul ogres after dragons devastated their original settlement to the south, the village serves as a tenuous stronghold surrounded by Alliance spies, deserters, and the black dragonflight.",h="Brackenwall Village is the primary Horde outpost in Dustwallow Marsh, nestled among the bogs in the northwest...",sec={{t="Refuge of the Stonemaul",b="When black dragonkin drove the Stonemaul ogres out of their ancient home at Stonemaul Village in the southern marsh, their leader, Overlord Mok'Morokk—successor to Rexxar—led the survivors north into the swamp to build Brackenwall. Formed around traditional earthen mounds, huts, and an old watchtower, the settlement gave the battered clan a defensible haven. Though aligned with the Horde, the village suffers from internal rot: Mok'Morokk sits idle, hoarding supplies and refusing to confront the draconic threat, leaving the clan's spiritual and tactical guidance to figures like the ogre mage Draz'Zilb and Horde emissaries.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Bog",b="Beyond internal dysfunction, Brackenwall is beset by external threats. Theramore infiltrators lurk constantly in the thickets, spying on village movements and reporting back to the island fortress. Meanwhile, Paval Reethe, a Theramore deserter cast out from Lost Point, is suspected of stealing vital supplies from the outpost. Between wary eyes watching from the east and black drakes prowling the southern reaches, Brackenwall serves as the Horde's isolated staging ground to keep both the Alliance and Onyxia's brood at bay.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are there ogres allied with the Horde here?",a="These are the Stonemaul ogres, an honorable clan inducted into the modern Horde by the champion Rexxar during the founding of Durotar. Rexxar became their chieftain after defeating their former leader, binding the clan to Warchief Thrall's new coalition before passing leadership to Mok'Morokk.",al={"why horde ogres","stonemaul clan lore","who are these ogres"}},{q="Why did the Stonemaul settle here instead of staying in their old home?",a="Their ancestral settlement in southern Dustwallow Marsh was overrun and obliterated by the black dragonflight. Overlord Mok'Morokk led the displaced survivors northward into the bog to establish Brackenwall as a fortified refuge.",al={"what happened to stonemaul village","why brackenwall","ogre refugees"}},{q="Who is in charge of Brackenwall Village?",a="Overlord Mok'Morokk leads the settlement, though his reign is widely resented. Rather than rallying his people to retake their homeland or confront the dragons, he cowers inside the village, forcing the ogre mage Draz'Zilb and Horde envoys to manage daily crises.",al={"brackenwall leader","who runs brackenwall","mok'morokk"}},{q="Why are there Theramore spies outside the village?",a="Despite the fragile truce between Theramore and Orgrimmar, Lady Jaina Proudmoore's military keeps close surveillance on any Horde troop movements within Dustwallow. Infiltrators skirt the perimeter of Brackenwall, reporting on ogre strength and Horde operations.",al={"alliance spies dustwallow","theramore infiltrators","why is theramore watching"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Brackenwall is your sole sanctuary and flight connection in the marsh; defending it ensures the Horde maintains a vital listening post and defensive flank against Theramore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Brackenwall is deep in hostile territory, but investigations concerning the missing diplomat and rogue Theramore deserters will bring daring agents right to the edge of the ogre encampment."},kw={"brackenwall","draz'zilb","dustwallow","infiltrators","mok'morokk","ogres","paval reethe","stonemaul"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","npc:overlord-mok-morokk","topic:horde","npc:onyxia","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:lost-point","quest:1241"},src={"Brackenwall Village"}}
E["subzone:darkmist-cavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkmist Cavern",z="dustwallow",s="Darkmist Cavern is an abandoned mine tucked into northwestern Dustwallow Marsh, completely infested with predatory giant spiders. Crumbling ruins outside hint at an unfortunate former settlement swallowed up by the marsh's hazards. Locals remain divided on whether the cavern gave its name to the arachnids or the reverse.",h="Darkmist Cavern is an abandoned mine tucked into northwestern Dustwallow Marsh, completely infested with...",sec={{t="The Brood in the Mine",b="Situated in the northwest reaches of Dustwallow Marsh, Darkmist Cavern appears to have once been an active mining venture. Today, any human presence has long vanished, leaving behind rotting, ruined shacks outside the entrance and a network of tunnels choked with thick webs. The cavern is overrun by Darkmist spiders, predatory horrors whose venom and size make the tunnels deadly to unwary wanderers. Marsh dwellers still dispute whether the cavern was named after the foul brood nesting inside or if the spiders took the title from the misty cave itself.",sp=0},{t="Hermit's Larder",b="Despite the obvious danger, the cavern attracts occasional scavengers and eccentric marshfolk. The hermit 'Swamp Eye' Jarl is notorious for sending travelers deep into the webs to harvest the eyes of these monstrous spiders, insisting they make a fine stock for broth. Aside from such eccentric culinary outings, most sensible travelers steer well clear of the web-strewn entrance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Darkmist Cavern?",a="It is an abandoned mine in northwestern Dustwallow Marsh that has fallen entirely into the possession of giant, venomous spiders known as Darkmist spiders.",al={"what is darkmist cavern","darkmist cave","spider cave dustwallow"}},{q="Who lived at the ruins outside the cave?",a="The small wooden ruins suggest a settlement or mining camp once operated here, but its former inhabitants are not identified.",al={"who lived here","houses outside darkmist cavern","abandoned village darkmist"}},{q="Why do locals venture into Darkmist Cavern?",a="Very few willingly enter, but the eccentric hermit 'Swamp Eye' Jarl hires daring adventurers to dive into the tunnels and retrieve spider eyes to brew into his strange marsh stew.",al={"why go to darkmist cavern","darkmist cavern quest"}},{q="Did the spiders or the cavern get the name first?",a="The inhabitants of Dustwallow Marsh disagree on whether the spiders were named after the cavern or the cavern after the spiders. No settled account establishes which name came first.",al={"spider name origin","why is it called darkmist"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The eccentric hermit 'Swamp Eye' Jarl considers the foul eyes of Darkmist spiders to be the prime ingredient for a hearty marsh stew, though few outside the swamp share his taste.",["profession:Mining"]="The cavern was clearly hollowed out by past miners, but anyone looking to prospect its rocky depths will have to fight through hordes of nesting spiders first."},kw={"darkmist cavern","darkmist spiders","dustwallow marsh","mine ruins","spider mine","swamp eye jarl"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","quest:938"},src={"Darkmist Cavern"}}
E["subzone:den-of-flame"] = {t="subzone",n="Den of Flame",z="dustwallow",s="The Den of Flame is a fortified cavern in western Dustwallow Marsh, situated just west of the Stonemaul Ruins. Originally constructed by the Stonemaul ogres as their mound, it has since been overrun by the dragonkin of the black dragonflight serving Onyxia.",h="The Den of Flame is a fortified cavern in western Dustwallow Marsh, situated just west of the Stonemaul Ruins.",sec={{t="A Conquered Mound",b="Built by the Stonemaul ogres to serve as their main mound and sanctuary, the Den of Flame bears the unmistakable, rough-hewn stone architecture of ogre masonry. However, when the black dragonflight laid waste to the Stonemaul clan's settlement, the brood did not merely scatter the ogres—they seized the stronghold for themselves. Today, black dragonspawn patrol the burning perimeter and cavern entrance under the shadow of Onyxia's nearby lair. Despite the infestation, vestiges of the former masters remain inside, including an abandoned Stonemaul clan banner left behind in the chaos.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Den of Flame originally built for?",a="The structure was originally built by the Stonemaul ogres to serve as their clan's primary mound. Its stonework and layout mirror classic ogre clan architecture.",al={"who built den of flame","den of flame origin","ogre mound dustwallow"}},{q="Why are black dragonkin infesting this mound?",a="The great black dragon Onyxia established her lair in the marsh nearby. Her dragonkin drove the Stonemaul ogres out of their settlement and claimed the cavern as a forward outpost for the brood.",al={"why are there dragons here","who lives in den of flame","dragonspawn dustwallow"}},{q="Can the Stonemaul ogres reclaim the cave?",a="The surviving Stonemaul ogres, now displaced to Brackenwall Village, still consider the cavern sacred ground. They seek brave champions to venture inside and recover their lost clan banner from the dragonspawn.",al={"stonemaul banner","reclaiming the den"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Stonemaul ogres are sworn allies of the Horde; clearing out the dragonkin and retrieving their clan banner from the Den of Flame helps avenge their fallen settlement."},kw={"black dragonflight","den of flame","dragonspawn","dustwallow marsh","onyxia","stonemaul banner","stonemaul ruins"},rel={"subzone:stonemaul-ruins","npc:onyxia","topic:black-dragonflight","zone:dustwallow"},src={"Den of Flame"}}
E["subzone:dragonmurk"] = {t="subzone",n="Dragonmurk",z="dustwallow",s="Dragonmurk is a sprawling, hazardous tract of southern Dustwallow Marsh swarming with black dragonspawn and hatchlings. Flanked by ancient ogre ruins and scorched caverns, it serves as the hostile outer perimeter for the brood of Onyxia.",h="Dragonmurk is a sprawling, hazardous tract of southern Dustwallow Marsh swarming with black dragonspawn and...",sec={{t="A Brood in the Bog",b="Spanning the southern interior of Dustwallow Marsh, the Dragonmurk marks the threshold where damp wetlands give way to the dominion of the black dragonflight. The waterways and thick mud here crawl with black wyrmkins, dragonspawn, and ravenous whelps. The surrounding landscape has suffered deeply from their presence; adjacent territories such as the ruined village of Stonemaul and the scorched cavern known as the Den of Flame have both fallen completely under the flight's territorial grip.",sp=0},{t="Guarding the Broodmother",b="The swarms of drakes and guards throughout the Dragonmurk are not random wanderers. Southern Dustwallow serves as the primary nesting ground in Kalimdor for Onyxia, the daughter of Deathwing. The wyrmkin patrol the mire aggressively, annihilating interlopers and protecting the clutch from both Theramore's scouts and the Horde's nearby encampments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Dragonmurk?",a="Dragonmurk is the southern region of Dustwallow Marsh that is heavily infested with whelps, drakes, and dragonspawn belonging to the black dragonflight.",al={"what is dragonmurk","where is dragonmurk","dragonmurk location"}},{q="Why are there so many black dragons here?",a="Southern Dustwallow Marsh contains the lair of Onyxia, a broodmother of the black dragonflight. Dragonmurk acts as a protective buffer where her offspring and servants can nest, mature, and ward off outside threats.",al={"why black dragons in dustwallow","who leads the dragons here","onyxia dragons dustwallow"}},{q="What landmarks are found near Dragonmurk?",a="Dragonmurk encompasses and surrounds key sites including the Den of Flame and the Stonemaul Ruins, both of which have been overrun and occupied by black dragonspawn.",al={"dragonmurk landmarks","what is near dragonmurk","places around dragonmurk"}},{q="Is Dragonmurk safe for travelers?",a="Not at all. The dragonkin in Dragonmurk are uniformly hostile and aggressive, making it one of the most perilous wilderness regions in southern Kalimdor.",al={"is dragonmurk dangerous","can i walk through dragonmurk"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The dragons in Dragonmurk drove the Stonemaul ogres from their village and continually endanger Horde expeditions venturing deep into the marsh.",["faction:Alliance"]="Theramore keeps a wary eye on the Dragonmurk, knowing that an unchecked black dragon brood so close to the fortress could easily spell disaster."},kw={"black dragonflight","den of flame","dragonmurk","dragonspawn","dustwallow marsh","onyxia","stonemaul ruins","whelps"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","topic:black-dragonflight","subzone:den-of-flame","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","quest:1089"},src={"Dragonmurk"}}
E["subzone:dreadmurk-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreadmurk Shore",z="dustwallow",s="Dreadmurk Shore encompasses the foggy coastline and scattered islands of Dustwallow Marsh running north toward the Barrens. Dominated by aggressive Mirefin murlocs and sea beasts, these treacherous waters have recently become the hiding ground for shipwrecked Defias Brotherhood outlaws.",h="Dreadmurk Shore encompasses the foggy coastline and scattered islands of Dustwallow Marsh running north...",sec={{t="A Treacherous Coast",b="Stretching along the northeastern edge of Dustwallow Marsh between Theramore Isle and Northwatch Hold, Dreadmurk Shore is a dismal expanse of muddy shoals, tide pools, and misty islands. The coast is overrun by the Mirefin tribe, a territorial clan of murlocs that aggressively attacks any travelers nearing their coastal villages. Sea turtles and aquatic predators prowl the shallows, making the shoreline dangerous to navigate even without factoring in the surrounding swamplands.",sp=0},{t="Defias Infiltrators",b="Beyond the indigenous swamp creatures, the shoreline has drawn heightened scrutiny from Theramore due to the presence of human outlaws. A ship bearing the Defias Brotherhood met disaster in the waters between the shore and Alcaz Island, spilling brigands onto the sand and islets. The presence of these Eastern Kingdoms criminals so close to Lady Jaina Proudmoore's stronghold is an alarming development that threatens the fragile balance of power across the bay.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Dreadmurk Shore located?",a="Dreadmurk Shore stretches along the northeastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh, facing the Great Sea between the outskirts of Theramore Isle and the border of the Barrens near Northwatch Hold.",al={"dreadmurk shore location","where is dreadmurk shore"}},{q="Why are there Defias bandits on this shore?",a="A Defias Brotherhood vessel recently wrecked in the waters offshore between Dreadmurk and Alcaz Island. The survivors scrambled ashore, establishing temporary camps along the isolated beach and outcroppings while trying to salvage their sunken cargo.",al={"defias in dustwallow","why are defias here","shipwrecked defias"}},{q="Who are the murlocs living along the beach?",a="The coast is heavily populated by the Mirefin murloc tribe. They have built crude fishing settlements along the sandbanks and rocky islets, fiercely guarding their territory from both Theramore patrols and shipwrecked intruders.",al={"mirefin murlocs","dreadmurk shore murlocs"}},{q="Is Dreadmurk Shore controlled by Theramore?",a="Theramore claims nominal authority over the lands surrounding the island, but Dreadmurk Shore is functionally lawless. Its marshy shoals are too wild and infested with murlocs and brigands for Lady Jaina Proudmoore's sentries to maintain regular patrols.",al={"who owns dreadmurk shore","is dreadmurk shore alliance"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The discovery of Defias Brotherhood survivors so close to Theramore suggests conspiracies that reach far beyond Westfall, directly threatening Alliance stability in Kalimdor.",["class:Rogue"]="The isolated camps and sunken wreckage along the shoreline offer prime opportunities to track clandestine Defias cargo and slip past the territory's violent Mirefin sentinels."},kw={"alcaz island","defias","dreadmurk shore","dustwallow marsh","mirefin","murloc","shipwreck","theramore"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:theramore-isle","topic:murloc","zone:barrens"},src={"Dreadmurk Shore"}}
E["subzone:dustwallow-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Dustwallow Bay",z="dustwallow",s="Dustwallow Bay is an inlet of the Great Sea tucked between the sodden coast of Dustwallow Marsh and the fortified port of Theramore Isle. Its brackish coastal shallows teem with marine life, treacherous shoals, and secluded coves just off the main maritime routes of eastern Kalimdor.",h="Dustwallow Bay is an inlet of the Great Sea tucked between the sodden coast of Dustwallow Marsh and the...",sec={{t="Waters of the Eastern Marsh",b="Dustwallow Bay defines the coastal boundary where the stagnant, murky wetlands of Dustwallow Marsh meet the open waters of the Great Sea. Flanked to the east by Theramore Isle, the bay serves as an oceanic approach for vessels arriving at Lady Jaina Proudmoore's island haven. Despite heavy maritime traffic running to and from the docks, the surrounding coastline remains wild and hazardous, pocked with rocky outcrops, murloc encampments, and tucked-away inlets like Tidefury Cove.",sp=0},{t="A Fisherman's Haven",b="While the marsh itself is infested with crocolisks and hostile beasts, the bay's islands and inlets draw those who seek isolation and rich catches. The small islets dotting the waters near Tidefury Cove provide a secluded retreat for anglers, most notably the legendary fisherman Nat Pagle, who can often be found angling off the rocks away from the bustling city of Theramore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Dustwallow Bay located?",a="Dustwallow Bay lies along the eastern coastline of central Kalimdor. It sits directly between the sodden eastern shores of Dustwallow Marsh and the rocky citadel of Theramore Isle.",al={"dustwallow bay location","where is dustwallow bay","dustwallow water"}},{q="Who can be found in the bay?",a="The most famous resident of the bay's outer reaches is Nat Pagle, the world-renowned angler. He makes his camp on a small islet tucked into nearby Tidefury Cove, just southwest of Theramore Isle.",al={"who is in dustwallow bay","nat pagle dustwallow bay","npcs dustwallow bay"}},{q="Is Dustwallow Bay safe to swim across?",a="While the bay is relatively close to the safety of Theramore Isle, its shallows and coastlines are frequented by murlocs, sharks, and other aggressive aquatic wildlife native to the marsh fringes.",al={"is dustwallow bay dangerous","monsters in dustwallow bay"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance sailors and travelers bound for Kalimdor, Dustwallow Bay is the final stretch of open sea before entering the fortified harbor of Theramore Isle."},kw={"dustwallow bay","dustwallow marsh","great sea","nat pagle","theramore","tidefury cove"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:tidefury-cove","npc:nat-pagle"},src={"Dustwallow Bay"}}
E["subzone:foothold-citadel"] = {t="subzone",n="Foothold Citadel",z="dustwallow",s="Foothold Citadel serves as the central military barracks and command post within Theramore Isle. Overlooking the fortified settlement, it houses the officers and guards who protect the Alliance's primary bastion on southern Kalimdor.",h="Foothold Citadel serves as the central military barracks and command post within Theramore Isle.",sec={{t="Heart of the Theramore Guard",b="Rising within the fortified stone walls of Theramore Isle, Foothold Citadel is the nerve center of local Alliance defense. The citadel houses the high command of the Theramore Guard, including Captain Garran Vimes and Commander Samaul, along with field medics, logistics officers, and quartermasters. Its utilitarian stone halls bustle with regular patrols and drills, keeping Lady Jaina Proudmoore's forces prepared against threats creeping out of the surrounding swamplands.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Admiral's Fall",b="The citadel bears a grim history tied to the founding days of Theramore. When Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore seized control of the city to wage his personal crusade against the Horde, this very fortress became the battleground of his final stand. Thrall's allied strike force, spearheaded by the Mok'Nathal warrior Rexxar, breached the citadel and struck the Admiral down. Today, the fortress stands repaired and steadfast, though the memory of that bloody conflict still hangs over its stone ramparts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Foothold Citadel used for?",a="Foothold Citadel functions as the headquarters and military barracks for the Theramore Guard. It houses command officers, tactical planners, training facilities, and logistics staff like the local paymaster and medical personnel.",al={"foothold citadel purpose","theramore barracks","what is this building"}},{q="What happened to Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore here?",a="During the conflict following the Third War, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore commandeered Theramore to wage war on the young Horde. A combined force led by the champion Rexxar stormed the citadel, slaying the Admiral in his own headquarters.",al={"daelin death","daelin proudmoore last stand","who killed daelin"}},{q="Who is currently in charge at Foothold Citadel?",a="Operational command of the garrison falls to officers like Captain Garran Vimes and Commander Samaul, who oversee daily patrols and regional security under the ultimate authority of Lady Jaina Proudmoore.",al={"who leads the citadel","theramore guard commander","citadel leader"}},{q="Can I receive medical aid inside the citadel?",a="Yes. Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen resides inside Foothold Citadel, tending to wounded guardsmen and instructing Alliance travelers in advanced field medicine and triage.",al={"citadel doctor","theramore medic","first aid trainer theramore"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The citadel is the primary military anchor for the Alliance in southern Kalimdor, coordinating defense against swamp beasts, Grimtotem marauders, and watchful Horde scouts.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Foothold Citadel is remembered as the site where Rexxar and Thrall brought an end to Grand Admiral Proudmoore's vengeful campaign to ensure Durotar's survival."},kw={"barracks","daelin proudmoore","dustwallow marsh","foothold citadel","garran vimes","gustaf vanhowzen","samaul","theramore"},rel={"subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","topic:alliance","npc:doctor-gustaf-vanhowzen","npc:thrall"},src={"Foothold Citadel"}}
E["subzone:lost-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Lost Point",z="dustwallow",s="Lost Point is a dilapidated wooden watchtower standing in western Dustwallow Marsh, originally constructed by Theramore's forces as an advance scout post. It has since fallen into disrepair and slipped from the control of Lady Jaina Proudmoore's guard, now serving as a hideout for rogue deserters.",h="Lost Point is a dilapidated wooden watchtower standing in western Dustwallow Marsh, originally constructed by...",sec={{t="A Forsaken Outpost",b="Erected by the expeditionary forces of Theramore to monitor traffic and threats emerging from the Barrens, Lost Point has long outlived its intended military function. The outpost has decayed under the relentless moisture of the marsh, its timber rotting and its defenses abandoned by regular troops. Instead of garrison sentries, the tower and its immediate surroundings are occupied by human deserters who broke away from Theramore's service, finding shelter in the isolated wilderness far from the discipline of the city's commanders.",sp=0},{t="Den of Deserters",b="The deserters ensconced at Lost Point answer to Balos Jacken, a disgruntled former soldier who has banded these rogues together. Their presence is far more than a simple matter of military insubordination. Jacken and his cohorts hold key testimonies regarding traitorous elements within Theramore's ranks, including the involvement of Private Hendel in a high-stakes conspiracy that reaches into the upper echelons of the Alliance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Lost Point?",a="Lost Point is a rundown watchtower built by the humans of Theramore in the western marshes of Dustwallow. Though meant to serve as an advance scout tower, it has been abandoned by the military and taken over by deserters.",al={"lost point overview","what is this tower","about lost point"}},{q="Who lives at Lost Point right now?",a="The tower and surrounding camp are currently inhabited by Theramore deserters. These renegade human soldiers have abandoned their oaths to Theramore and operate under the leadership of Balos Jacken.",al={"who is at lost point","lost point enemies","lost point mobs"}},{q="Who is Balos Jacken?",a="Balos Jacken is the ringleader of the Theramore deserters hiding at Lost Point. Despite his criminal standing, he possesses crucial intelligence about troubling matters within Theramore's ranks.",al={"balos jacken","deserter leader","who leads lost point"},sp=1},{q="Why did Theramore abandon the tower?",a="Dustwallow Marsh is hostile and difficult to supply. As garrison morale broke and discipline strained, the isolated outpost fell into disrepair, becoming an ideal sanctuary for soldiers seeking to escape duty without fleeing into Horde territory.",al={"why abandoned","why is lost point ruined","why run down"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance loyalists, Lost Point is a bitter symbol of fraying discipline within Theramore's ranks and a den of renegades harboring dark secrets about military treason."},kw={"balos jacken","dustwallow marsh","lost point","scout tower","theramore deserters"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},src={"Lost Point"}}
E["subzone:nat-s-landing"] = {t="subzone",n="Nat's Landing",z="dustwallow",s="Nat's Landing is a modest fishing outpost nestled along the shores of Dustwallow Bay in Dustwallow Marsh. It serves as the personal camp and retreat of Nat Pagle, widely regarded as the most famous angler on Azeroth. Adventurers from across the world seek out this humble dock to hone their mastery of the fishing craft.",h="Nat's Landing is a modest fishing outpost nestled along the shores of Dustwallow Bay in Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="A Master's Haven",b="Tucked away southwest of Theramore Isle along the murky waters of Dustwallow Bay, Nat's Landing is little more than a weathered campsite. It consists of a simple canvas tent, drying racks heavy with the day's catch, extra tackle hung from trees, and a rickety wooden pier jutting into the bay. Despite the mists and hazards of the swamp, this quiet patch of shoreline provides the legendary angler Nat Pagle with a solitary place to cast his line and enjoy a quiet drink away from civilization's clamor.",sp=0},{t="The Fisherman's Pilgrimage",b="Though unassuming at a glance, the landing is an essential stop for aspiring anglers. Fishermen who have exhausted the teachings of standard trainers in Ironforge, Orgrimmar, or elsewhere are directed here to prove their worth directly to Nat. Pagle cares nothing for politics or factional squabbles; any angler who braves the marshland predators to reach his dock must demonstrate patience and skill across the world's most perilous waters to earn his highest instruction.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Nat's Landing located?",a="Nat's Landing is situated on a small coastal outcrop along the waters of Dustwallow Bay, in the eastern stretches of Dustwallow Marsh just southwest of Theramore Isle.",al={"where is nats landing","nats landing location","how to get to nats landing"}},{q="Who lives at Nat's Landing?",a="The landing is the personal campsite of Nat Pagle, the renowned human angler who spends his days fishing off the pier with a drink in hand.",al={"who is at nats landing","nats landing npc","who lives here"}},{q="Why do anglers travel here?",a="When anglers have mastered all their local trainers can teach them in major capitals, they are sent to Nat Pagle. He tests their dedication with challenging catches around the world before granting them artisan-level instruction.",al={"why come to nats landing","artisan fishing trainer","nat pagle training"}},{q="Does Nat Pagle welcome both Alliance and Horde?",a="Yes. Nat Pagle is neutral toward dedicated anglers, welcoming both Alliance travelers from Theramore and Horde travelers venturing in from the Barrens, regardless of faction loyalties.",al={"is nats landing hostile","can horde talk to nat","is nat pagle neutral"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance citizens stationed in Theramore, Nat's Landing is a short, quiet walk down the coast, offering easy access to the world's premier fisherman.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde anglers trekking across the perilous swamp from the Barrens will find Nat indifferent to the war, judging visitors solely by the quality of their cast."},kw={"angler","dock","dustwallow bay","dustwallow marsh","fishing","nat pagle","nats landing","theramore"},rel={"npc:nat-pagle","zone:dustwallow","subzone:dustwallow-bay","quest:6608","subzone:zul-gurub","zone:ironforge","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Nat's Landing"}}
E["subzone:onyxia-s-lair"] = {t="subzone",n="Onyxia's Lair",z="dustwallow",s="Onyxia's Lair is a subterranean cavern located deep within the Wyrmbog of Dustwallow Marsh. It serves as the nesting sanctuary and stronghold for Onyxia, broodmother of the black dragonflight. Inside its sweltering, magma-filled chambers, the great dragon watches over clutches of black dragon eggs.",h="Onyxia's Lair is a subterranean cavern located deep within the Wyrmbog of Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="A Den of Magma and Ruin",b="Carved into the treacherous mud and petrified wood of the Wyrmbog, the cavern entrance resembles the yawning maw of a dragon. Within, the cool rot of the marsh gives way to intense volcanic heat. Magma seeps from cracks in the obsidian stone, while subterranean tremors routinely shake the ceilings. The central chamber opens into a vast incubator where hundreds of black dragon eggs lie nested amid ash and embers, overseen by flightkin, dragonspawn guards, and Onyxia herself.",sp=0},{t="The Broodmother's Retreat",b="While Onyxia's brother Nefarian plots across the sea from Blackrock Spire, Onyxia has long maintained this secluded roost on Kalimdor to breed the next generation of the black dragonflight. The lair acts as a redoubt when her intricate political schemes unravel. Here, far from the courts of mortal kingdoms, she can abandon her human guises and take her true, terrible form as daughter of Deathwing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where exactly is Onyxia's Lair?",a="The lair is situated in southern Dustwallow Marsh within the Wyrmbog, just south of the Dragonmurk. The entrance is marked by massive dragon bones, smoldering terrain, and black dragonkin sentries guarding a stony fissure shaped like an open jaw.",al={"where is onyxia","onyxia location","how to find onyxia lair","dragonmurk cave"}},{q="What creatures dwell inside the lair?",a="The cavern is inhabited almost entirely by members of the black dragonflight. Broodmother Onyxia commands the deep chamber, surrounded by swarms of freshly hatched whelps, guardian dragonspawn, and mature black drakes.",al={"onyxia lair mobs","who lives in onyxia lair","what is inside"}},{q="Why is the cave so hot if it sits in a swamp?",a="Onyxia dug her lair deep into Kalimdor's crust, tapping into subterranean veins of magma. The extreme volcanic heat provides the scorching conditions necessary to incubate black dragon eggs, contrasting sharply with the cold mud of Dustwallow Marsh above.",al={"why is there lava in dustwallow","onyxia lair volcano"}},{q="Why is Onyxia hiding out in Kalimdor?",a="Dustwallow Marsh offers isolation and concealment. Its thick fogs, dismal quagmires, and dangerous wildlife keep mortal armies away, allowing the broodmother to replenish her flight's numbers undisturbed while she coordinates her covert meddling abroad.",al={"why is onyxia here","why dustwallow marsh","onyxia kalimdor"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions, this cavern is the den of a black broodmother whose growing brood threatens Theramore and every settlement around the marsh.",["faction:Horde"]="Dustwallow Marsh borders Horde territory in the Barrens and Mulgore; allowing a black broodmother to hatch an army of dragons on Kalimdor poses an existential threat to all of the new Horde."},kw={"black dragonflight","broodmother","dragonmurk","dustwallow","lair","onyxia","whelps","wyrmbog"},rel={"npc:onyxia","subzone:dragonmurk","zone:dustwallow","topic:black-dragonflight","subzone:wyrmbog","npc:deathwing","zone:stormwind"},src={"Onyxia's Lair"}}
E["subzone:quagmire"] = {t="subzone",n="Quagmire",z="dustwallow",s="The Quagmire comprises the sprawling, treacherous heart of central Dustwallow Marsh. Bound by Brackenwall Village to the north and the Dragonmurk to the south, its waterlogged flats are notoriously difficult to navigate. Hostile beasts and ravenous oozes make any journey through this central fen perilous.",h="The Quagmire comprises the sprawling, treacherous heart of central Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="Heart of the Fen",b="Occupying the wide expanse between Lost Point in the west and Dustwallow Bay in the east, the Quagmire represents the wild core of the marsh. Footing is unreliable at best, with solid earth constantly giving way to murky water and clinging mud. Travelers must contend with predatory crocolisks lurking beneath the scum, aggressive spiders nesting in the dead brush, and strange oozes that seep through the muck.",sp=0},{t="Encroaching Clashes",b="Beyond its natural hazards, the Quagmire serves as an unpredictable crossroads for the sentient powers contesting the swamp. Tucked away within the bog lies Tabetha's Farm, a lonely refuge for practitioners seeking hermit wisdom amid the dangers of the swamp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Quagmire located?",a="The Quagmire covers the central portion of Dustwallow Marsh. It stretches west toward Lost Point, east toward Dustwallow Bay, north to the borders of Brackenwall Village, and south where the land descends into the Dragonmurk.",al={"quagmire location","where is the quagmire","quagmire map"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Deep in the fen lies Tabetha's Farm, a vital destination for aspiring mages seeking esoteric training far from the scrutiny of the Kirin Tor."},kw={"beezil","crocolisk","dustwallow","quagmire","tabetha"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:dragonmurk","subzone:tabetha-s-farm","subzone:beezil-s-wreck","subzone:lost-point","topic:tauren"},src={"Quagmire"}}
E["subzone:sentry-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Sentry Point",z="dustwallow",s="Sentry Point is a human watchtower stationed on the mainland edge of Dustwallow Marsh, guarding the causeway bridge that leads directly to Theramore Isle. Maintained by Theramore's forces, it monitors traffic entering and exiting Lady Jaina Proudmoore's island citadel.",h="Sentry Point is a human watchtower stationed on the mainland edge of Dustwallow Marsh, guarding the causeway...",sec={{t="The Gates of Theramore",b="Positioned at the western end of the long bridge linking Theramore Isle to the treacherous wetlands of Dustwallow Marsh, Sentry Point serves as the stronghold's first line of defense on the mainland. The stone scout tower keeps watch over the swamp road, ensuring that hostile marsh beasts, wandering Grimtotem tauren, or Horde raiders cannot approach the island city unnoticed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Sentry Point used for?",a="It serves as an early warning post and border checkpoint for Theramore Isle. The guards stationed here monitor traffic traveling the swamp road and alert the city guards to approaching threats.",al={"sentry point purpose","what is this tower","why is sentry point here"}},{q="Who controls this outpost?",a="The outpost is manned and maintained by the Theramore Guard, operating under the command of Lady Jaina Proudmoore and her military officers.",al={"who owns sentry point","is sentry point alliance","theramore guard tower"}},{q="Is Sentry Point safe for Horde travelers?",a="No. While Lady Jaina Proudmoore strives for peace with the Horde, the military guards stationed at this outpost protect Alliance territory and will attack trespassing Horde members on sight.",al={"can horde go to sentry point","horde friendly sentry point"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For travelers coming from the perilous bogs of Dustwallow Marsh, Sentry Point marks the welcoming threshold to the safety of Theramore Isle.",["faction:Horde"]="The tower serves as a stark reminder of Theramore's military presence on the Kalimdor mainland, heavily guarded against any approaching Horde scouts."},kw={"bridge","dustwallow marsh","guard tower","jaina proudmoore","sentry point","theramore","watchtower"},rel={"subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","npc:jaina-proudmoore"},src={"Sentry Point"}}
E["subzone:shady-rest-inn"] = {t="subzone",n="Shady Rest Inn",z="dustwallow",s="The Shady Rest Inn was once a welcoming human-built waystation sitting just off the road between the Barrens and Theramore Isle. Today, only charred timbers and smoldering ashes remain following a sudden and violent arson attack. The tragedy left the innkeeper shattered and sparked tension across the marsh as investigators sift through the wreckage for clues.",h="The Shady Rest Inn was once a welcoming human-built waystation sitting just off the road between the Barrens...",sec={{t="Ashes on the Border",b="Built to serve travelers navigating the treacherous crossing between Dustwallow Marsh and the Barrens, the Shady Rest Inn stood as an outpost of civilized comfort in a harsh wilderness. That ended when the inn was abruptly razed to the ground in a devastating fire. Innkeeper James Hyal managed to survive the inferno, but the blaze claimed the lives of his wife and child. Traumatized and grief-stricken, Hyal was left with nothing as the ruins became an active crime scene, drawing scrutiny from Theramore authorities desperate to identify who ignited the flames.",sp=0},{t="A Web of Suspicion",b="Initial inquiries into the arson pointed toward human deserters and suspicious soldiers, with figures such as Paval Reethe and Lieutenant Caldwell falling under heavy suspicion before meeting untimely ends. However, physical evidence recovered from the ashes—including distinctive hoofprints and ritual badges—revealed that the attack was not merely an act of internal treachery. The arson was carried out by the ruthless Grimtotem tauren, who strike from the deep marsh to sow discord between Theramore and its neighbors.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the Shady Rest Inn?",a="The inn was attacked and burned to the ground. Deserters and rogue Alliance soldiers were initially suspected, and investigators are still sifting the ashes for clues to who was truly behind the arson.",al={"why is shady rest inn burned","what happened to the inn","who burned shady rest"},sp=1},{q="Who owned and operated the inn?",a="James Hyal ran the Shady Rest Inn. He survived the blaze, but his wife and child perished in the flames, leaving him deeply traumatized.",al={"innkeeper shady rest","who ran shady rest","james hyal"}},{q="Where is the Shady Rest Inn located?",a="The ruins lie along the main road in western Dustwallow Marsh, right near the border where the marsh gives way to the Barrens.",al={"shady rest location","where is shady rest inn"}},{q="Who are Paval Reethe and Lieutenant Caldwell?",a="They were human suspects implicated during the early investigation into the fire. Both died before investigators could extract confessions or definitively uncover the full extent of their involvement.",al={"who is reethe","lieutenant caldwell shady rest","reethe and caldwell"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The destruction of the inn represents a severe security breach on the main overland route to Theramore Isle, threatening travelers and inflaming fears of hidden enemies.",["race:Tauren"]="The Grimtotem clan's violent, unprovoked raid threatens to shatter the fragile peace between the Horde and Jaina Proudmoore's forces in Dustwallow Marsh."},kw={"arson","barrens border","dustwallow marsh","grimtotem","james hyal","paval reethe","shady rest inn","theramore"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","topic:tauren"},src={"Shady Rest Inn"}}
E["subzone:stonemaul-ruins"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonemaul Ruins",z="dustwallow",s="The Stonemaul Ruins are the shattered remnants of Stonemaul Village, once the proud Kalimdor settlement of the Stonemaul ogres. After being driven out by the black dragonflight, the clan fled north, leaving their former home overrun by Firemane dragonspawn.",h="The Stonemaul Ruins are the shattered remnants of Stonemaul Village, once the proud Kalimdor settlement of...",sec={{t="Rise and Fall of the Clan Home",b="Following their migration to Kalimdor, the Stonemaul ogres founded their settlement amid the murky swamps of Dustwallow Marsh. The village became famous when the beastmaster Rexxar braved the clan's lethal trials, slew their brutal chieftain Kor'gall, and rallied the ogres to defend the nascent Horde against Admiral Proudmoore's forces. After the war, Rexxar left the ogre Mok'Morokk in command. Under Mok'Morokk's selfish rule, the village fell into decline and was ultimately ambushed and shattered by the black dragonflight. The surviving ogres fled north to establish Brackenwall Village, while Onyxia's brood took complete possession of the ruins.",sp=0},{t="The Struggle for Reclamation",b="Today, the ruins are firmly ensconced within Dragonmurk and crawl with Firemane dragonspawn tending the brood's nearby nesting grounds. While Overlord Mok'Morokk grew cowardly and content to languish in Brackenwall, older and prouder clan members like Tharg and Draz'Zilb refuse to abandon their homeland. Operating out of Brackenwall, they urge Horde champions to slaughter the occupying dragonspawn and smash the dragonflight's eggs in hopes that the Stonemaul may one day march back and reclaim their ancestral village.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who used to live in Stonemaul Ruins?",a="The Stonemaul clan of ogres built and inhabited the settlement, then known as Stonemaul Village, after arriving on Kalimdor.",al={"who lived here","stonemaul ruins history","who built stonemaul village"}},{q="Why was the village abandoned?",a="Onyxia's black dragonflight assaulted the settlement and drove the ogres out, turning the village into a nesting outpost for Firemane dragonspawn.",al={"why is stonemaul destroyed","what happened to stonemaul village","who attacked stonemaul"}},{q="Where did the surviving ogres go?",a="The survivors retreated north into Dustwallow Marsh under Overlord Mok'Morokk and established Brackenwall Village as their temporary stronghold.",al={"where are the ogres now","stonemaul ogre location"}},{q="What was Rexxar's connection to this place?",a="Rexxar came here to enlist the ogres against Kul Tiras. He bested their trial, slew their tyrannical warlord Kor'gall in combat, and briefly served as chieftain before passing leadership to Mok'Morokk.",al={"rexxar stonemaul","rexxar ogre chieftain"}},{q="Do the ogres plan to retake the ruins?",a="Yes. While Mok'Morokk was afraid to act, other Stonemaul leaders like Tharg and Draz'Zilb actively recruit Horde adventurers to culled the Firemane dragonspawn and prepare for retaking their home.",al={"will the ogres go back","retaking stonemaul"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Stonemaul ogres are staunch allies who shed blood alongside Thrall's Horde against Kul Tiras. Helping them strike back against the black dragonflight honors that pact."},kw={"brackenwall","dragonmurk","firemane","kor'gall","mok'morokk","stonemaul","stonemaul ruins","stonemaul village"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:dragonmurk","npc:overlord-mok-morokk","npc:onyxia","topic:black-dragonflight","topic:horde","zone:dustwallow"},src={"Stonemaul Ruins"}}
E["subzone:swamplight-manor"] = {t="subzone",n="Swamplight Manor",z="dustwallow",s="Swamplight Manor is an ironically named, ramshackle wooden shack nestled deep within Witch Hill in Dustwallow Marsh. It serves as the eccentric home and kitchen of 'Swamp Eye' Jarl, an isolated recluse known across the mire for his strange culinary appetites. Despite its humble, eerie isolation, the surrounding garden conceals intrigue that catches the attention of both Theramore and Brackenwall Village.",h="Swamplight Manor is an ironically named, ramshackle wooden shack nestled deep within Witch Hill in Dustwallow...",sec={{t="A Hermit's Respite in the Mire",b="Despite what its grandiose title suggests, Swamplight Manor is far from a lordly estate. It is merely a crooked, weather-beaten shack tucked into the haunted wetlands of Witch Hill. Its lone resident, the odd recluse known as 'Swamp Eye' Jarl, lives a solitary existence surrounded by fog, muck, and restless marsh ghosts. Jarl spends his days concocting unusual regional delicacies out of local wildlife, frequently recruiting wandering adventurers to hunt down bizarre ingredients like marsh frog legs and creature eyes to satisfy his strange craft.",sp=0},{t="Secrets in the Garden",b="While travelers usually stumble upon the manor seeking eccentric cooking or shelter from the spirits of Witch Hill, the grounds conceal a much darker border conflict. Buried under a loose pile of dirt in Jarl's makeshift garden lies a discarded orcish spy's report, complete with a severed head nearby. Both the Theramore guards under Captain Garran Vimes and the Horde forces at Brackenwall Village have keen interests in recovering these documents, making the hermit's patch of overgrown soil an unexpected flashpoint in the regional cold war.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is a tiny shack called a 'Manor'?",a="The name is purely ironic. The structure is little more than a soggy, rundown wooden hovel, named with a touch of eccentricity by its reclusive inhabitant, 'Swamp Eye' Jarl, to contrast with the dreary gloom of Witch Hill.",al={"swamplight manor name origin","why manor","is swamplight a real manor"}},{q="Who lives at Swamplight Manor?",a="'Swamp Eye' Jarl lives here alone. He is an infamous, half-crazed hermit and cook who chooses to dwell isolated in the haunted mire, hiring passing travelers to supply him with peculiar culinary ingredients and aid with the local spirits.",al={"who is swamp eye jarl","swamplight manor resident","who lives here"}},{q="What is buried in the garden outside?",a="Hidden in a pile of disturbed earth in Jarl's yard is a lost spy report penned by an orc, along with a severed head. Both Alliance authorities in Theramore and Horde scouts from Brackenwall Village are anxious to secure this intelligence.",al={"swamplight manor dirt pile","loose dirt swamplight","orc spy report"},sp=1},{q="Can both Alliance and Horde players visit Jarl?",a="Yes. Jarl lives so far removed from civilization that he maintains neutrality, gladly accepting help or trading recipes with both Alliance and Horde travelers.",al={"is jarl neutral","can horde talk to swamp eye jarl","swamplight faction"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="For culinarians braving the marshlands, Jarl represents the eccentric pinnacle of swamp foraging, crafting regional meals out of creatures most chefs would dread to touch.",["faction:Alliance"]="Theramore scouts sent by Captain Garran Vimes keep a watchful eye on rumors surrounding the manor, particularly concerning missing scouts and intercepted Horde correspondence."},kw={"brackenwall village","dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","lost report","swamp eye jarl","swamplight manor","witch hill"},rel={"subzone:witch-hill","zone:dustwallow","subzone:brackenwall-village","quest:165","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Swamplight Manor"}}
E["subzone:tabetha-s-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Tabetha's Farm",z="dustwallow",s="Deep in the murkiest reaches of the Quagmire lies Tabetha's Farm, an isolated homestead centered around a small wooden hut, a modest garden, and a private dock. Despite the treacherous marsh surroundings, this sanctuary serves as a hidden redoubt for the hermit mage Tabetha.",h="Deep in the murkiest reaches of the Quagmire lies Tabetha's Farm, an isolated homestead centered around a...",sec={{t="A Hermit's Sanctuary",b="Tucked away in the western wetlands of Dustwallow Marsh, Tabetha's Farm defies its unforgiving environment. Consisting of a weather-worn hut, small vegetable plots, and a dock for navigating the swamp's murky waterways, the homestead offers a quiet refuge far from the political rivalries of Theramore and Brackenwall Village. Here, the reclusive human sorceress Tabetha lives in near-total seclusion, pursuing esoteric studies of arcane and fel power without interference from Dalaran or local authorities.",sp=0},{t="A Waypoint of Arcane Power",b="Despite its remote location, the farm attracts practitioners of the magical arts from across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. Mages seeking mastery over raw arcane surges and warlocks seeking aid to cleanse volatile artifacts like the Orb of Orahil are directed to Tabetha's doorstep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives at Tabetha's Farm?",a="The farm is home to the eccentric mage Tabetha, who keeps the small garden, dock, and homestead amidst the perilous swamp creatures of the Quagmire.",al={"who is tabetha","who lives here","inhabitants of tabetha's farm"}},{q="Why do mages travel all the way to this farm?",a="Mage trainers across the world direct promising students to Tabetha to further their arcane knowledge. She possesses deep expertise regarding volatile mana surges, ancient relics, and primal powers that standard city academies rarely teach.",al={"why do mages visit tabetha","mage quest dustwallow","mage class quest tabetha"}},{q="Why would warlocks come here?",a="Warlocks seek out Tabetha's expertise in exorcism and elemental energies when working to purify and tame dangerous artifacts, most notably during the rituals required to cleanse the Orb of Orahil.",al={"tabetha warlock quest","cleansing orb of orahil","warlock tabetha"}},{q="Is Tabetha's Farm allied with the Horde or the Alliance?",a="Tabetha maintains a neutral stance, offering her wisdom to travelers regardless of their political allegiance. Her farm remains independent of both Jaina Proudmoore's Theramore and the Horde forces at Brackenwall Village.",al={"is tabetha alliance","is tabetha horde","is tabetha neutral"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Your trainers in the capital cities hold Tabetha's esoteric knowledge in high esteem, sending adept spellcasters to her farm to investigate volatile mana surges and ancient relics of power.",["class:Warlock"]="Though she lives as a quiet swamp hermit, Tabetha is one of the few spellcasters capable of assisting you in cleansing the potent energies bound to the Orb of Orahil."},kw={"dustwallow","dustwallow marsh","quagmire","tabetha","tabetha's farm","tabetha's hut"},rel={"npc:tabetha","subzone:quagmire","zone:dustwallow","quest:2300","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:uldaman"},src={"Tabetha's Farm"}}
E["subzone:theramore-isle"] = {t="subzone",n="Theramore Isle",z="dustwallow",s="Theramore Isle is a heavily fortified human port citadel off the eastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh. Founded by Lady Jaina Proudmoore for refugees escaping the fall of Lordaeron, it stands as the Alliance's primary bastion in southern Kalimdor.",h="Theramore Isle is a heavily fortified human port citadel off the eastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="Refuge of the West",b="Following the devastation of Dalaran and Lordaeron by the Scourge during the Third War, Lady Jaina Proudmoore guided a fleet of survivors across the Great Sea to the shores of Kalimdor. After fighting alongside orcs and night elves to defeat the Burning Legion atop Mount Hyjal, her coalition of humans, dwarves, and high elves retreated to the misty fringes of Dustwallow Marsh. On a jagged island just off the coast, they built Theramore Isle—a thriving harbor city anchored by towering stone ramparts and Jaina's personal citadel, created to safeguard what remained of the northern kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="An Uneasy Peace",b="Theramore's history has been steeped in tension with Thrall's neighboring Horde in Durotar. When Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore arrived with the Kul Tiras fleet, he commandeered the isle and waged an unprovoked campaign to eradicate the orcs. Refusing to let hatred undo Kalimdor's hard-won survival, Jaina stood aside, allowing the Horde to strike down her father within Theramore's walls to preserve the peace. Today, the city maintains a fragile truce with Durotar, though simmering resentment among veteran sailors and covert agitation from the Burning Blade cult threaten to tear that delicate pact apart.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules Theramore Isle?",a="Lady Jaina Proudmoore governs Theramore Isle. A master sorceress originally from Dalaran and Kul Tiras, she led the survivors of Lordaeron to Kalimdor during the Third War and oversees both the city's military defense and its diplomatic relations.",al={"who leads theramore","theramore ruler","jaina theramore"}},{q="Why did humans build a city in a swamp?",a="Following the Battle of Mount Hyjal, the surviving human expedition needed a defensible coastal position to shelter their people and maintain a navy. The rocky island off Dustwallow Marsh offered deep-water anchorage and natural isolation from mainland threats, making it an ideal stronghold despite the miserable surrounding bog.",al={"why dustwallow","why is theramore in a marsh","why build here"}},{q="Is Theramore hostile to the Horde?",a="Theramore is an Alliance stronghold, making its guards hostile to Horde travelers on sight. However, officially Lady Jaina Proudmoore and Warchief Thrall maintain an uneasy diplomatic peace, respecting each other's territorial boundaries despite lingering hatred among their citizens.",al={"can horde visit theramore","theramore horde relations","are theramore humans at war"}},{q="What happened to Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore here?",a="Admiral Daelin Proudmoore seized Theramore from his daughter Jaina to wage war against the nascent Horde. Recognizing his campaign would destroy them all, Jaina stepped aside, allowing Thrall and Rexxar to storm the island citadel and slay the Admiral in battle.",al={"daelin death","what happened to jaina's father","daelin proudmoore theramore"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Theramore Isle serves as the primary seat of Alliance power in central Kalimdor, offering safety, vital ferry connections, and a well-defended harbor surrounded by hostile wilderness.",["class:Mage"]="As the personal domain of Archmage Jaina Proudmoore, Theramore holds powerful arcane conduits, serving as a vital nexus for Kirin Tor tradition and teleportation in the western hemisphere."},kw={"alliance","daelin proudmoore","dustwallow marsh","jaina proudmoore","kul tiras","lordaeron refugees","theramore"},rel={"npc:jaina-proudmoore","zone:dustwallow","topic:kul-tiras","npc:thrall","topic:alliance","topic:third-war","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:ratchet"},src={"Theramore Isle"}}
E["subzone:tidefury-cove"] = {t="subzone",n="Tidefury Cove",z="dustwallow",s="Tidefury Cove is a treacherous stretch of water and rocky shallows along the southeastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh, south of Theramore Isle. Renowned for its hazardous reefs and wrecked vessels, it serves as a secluded haven for roaming makrura and solitary anglers.",h="Tidefury Cove is a treacherous stretch of water and rocky shallows along the southeastern coast of Dustwallow...",sec={{t="A Graveyard of Ships and Reefs",b="Tucked away at the far end of Dustwallow Bay between Theramore Isle and the Wyrmbog, Tidefury Cove presents a notorious navigational hazard to passing sailors. Jagged reefs and shifting shoals have claimed multiple vessels over the years, leaving rotting wooden hulks half-submerged in the tideline. Today, the ruined ships are crawled over by opportunistic makrura, turning the cove into a dangerous, isolated stretch of coastline visited mostly by hardy scavengers or quiet hermits seeking distance from Theramore's busy docks.",sp=0},{t="The Historic Foothold",b="During the invasion of Durotar, the shores of Tidefury Cove became a crucial strategic battleground. Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiran expedition fortified the coast with an imposing coastal fortress and guard towers to command the approaches to Theramore. To break Proudmoore's grip, Thrall marshaled the combined strength of the young Horde—uniting orcs, Darkspear trolls, and tauren alongside Rexxar and the Stonemaul ogres—to storm the shoreline and dismantle the Kul Tiran beachhead before pressing directly toward the island fortress.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Tidefury Cove located?",a="Tidefury Cove sits along the southeastern edge of Dustwallow Marsh, just south of Theramore Isle and bordering the Wyrmbog coast at the southern end of Dustwallow Bay.",al={"tidefury cove location","where is tidefury cove","tidefury cove map"}},{q="Why are there shipwrecks in Tidefury Cove?",a="The cove is filled with shallow sandbars and hidden rocky reefs that make navigation extremely hazardous. Ships that stray too close to the coast frequently run aground, where waves and scavengers quickly reduce them to broken hulls.",al={"tidefury shipwrecks","broken ships tidefury","sunken ships dustwallow bay"}},{q="Who lives in Tidefury Cove today?",a="Aside from aggressive shoreline makrura, the cove's most notable resident is the famed angler Nat Pagle, who maintains an encampment known as Nat's Landing on one of the outer islets.",al={"who is in tidefury cove","tidefury cove residents","nat pagle location"}},{q="What battle took place here in the past?",a="During Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's campaign against the new Horde, Kul Tiran forces built a heavily fortified coastal stronghold here. Thrall's Horde, bolstered by tauren and ogre allies, assaulted and destroyed the base to clear the way to Theramore Isle.",al={"battle of tidefury cove","warcraft 3 tidefury","invasion of durotar tidefury"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, this coastline was the launching point for the final counter-offensive that broke Grand Admiral Proudmoore's naval aggression and secured the young nation's survival.",["profession:Cooking"]="The rich coastal shallows and proximity to master angler Nat Pagle make this stretch of Dustwallow a prime destination for fishermen seeking prized catches."},kw={"cove","dustwallow","makrura","pagle","proudmoore","reefs","shipwreck","theramore","tidefury"},rel={"subzone:dustwallow-bay","subzone:nat-s-landing","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:wyrmbog","zone:dustwallow","npc:nat-pagle","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},src={"Tidefury Cove"}}
E["subzone:witch-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Witch Hill",z="dustwallow",s="Witch Hill is a dreary, mist-shrouded rise in the heart of Dustwallow Marsh along the path toward Theramore. It is best known for the secluded Swamplight Manor, scattered camps of hostile Mirefin murlocs, and sinister rumors of dark hauntings.",h="Witch Hill is a dreary, mist-shrouded rise in the heart of Dustwallow Marsh along the path toward Theramore.",sec={{t="A Blighted Rise",b="Rising out of the stagnant waters of Dustwallow Marsh, Witch Hill sits roughly a third of the way along the peninsula leading southeast toward Theramore Isle. The elevated ground provides little refuge from the hazards of the swamp, as aggressive Mirefin murlocs claim the surrounding waters. At its center stands Swamplight Manor, the lonely and unsettling residence of the hermit known as 'Swamp Eye' Jarl. Travelers passing through frequently report eerie phenomena and lingering dark presences across the knoll.",sp=0},{t="The Haunting of the Hill",b="Behind its quiet, gloomy exterior, Witch Hill is steeped in dark rumor. Tales of hauntings cling to the desolate ground, adding to the local paranoia. Those who brave the hill must contend not only with the primitive savagery of the Mirefin, but with occult threats that make even seasoned Theramore patrols uneasy.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Witch Hill located?",a="Witch Hill is located in Dustwallow Marsh, situated about a third of the way down the peninsula that connects the western marsh to Theramore Isle.",al={"witch hill location","where is witch hill","how to find witch hill"}},{q="Who lives on Witch Hill?",a="The most prominent resident is 'Swamp Eye' Jarl, an eccentric hermit living inside Swamplight Manor near the hill's center. The surrounding lowlands are also infested by camps of Mirefin murlocs.",al={"who lives here","witch hill inhabitants","swamplight manor resident"}},{q="Why is the area called Witch Hill?",a="The knoll has long had a sinister reputation for dark magic, odd lights, and supernatural danger, compounded by the eerie solitude of Swamplight Manor.",al={"why witch hill","is there a witch here","witch hill lore"},sp=1},{q="What threats should travelers look out for on Witch Hill?",a="Travelers must beware of roaming Mirefin murlocs establishing camps around the hill, as well as the unsettling rumors of hauntings that cling to the hill.",al={"witch hill dangers","witch hill enemies","mobs on witch hill"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks passing along the Theramore road may sense the dark rumors of hauntings clinging to the dreary knoll.",["faction:Alliance"]="Witch Hill borders the primary overland route toward Theramore Isle, making its murloc tribes and dark entities an ongoing nuisance for travelers and couriers."},kw={"dustwallow marsh","mirefin","swamp eye jarl","swamplight manor","witch hill"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:swamplight-manor","topic:murloc"},src={"Witch Hill"}}
E["subzone:wyrmbog"] = {t="subzone",n="Wyrmbog",z="dustwallow",s="Wyrmbog is the perilous southern expanse of Dustwallow Marsh, lying just south of the Dragonmurk. Dominated by foul mire and jagged spires of stone, it serves as the staging ground and territorial buffer for the black dragonflight. The caves of ancient wyrms, including the broodmother Onyxia and the elder Emberstrife, are carved directly into its surrounding ridges.",h="Wyrmbog is the perilous southern expanse of Dustwallow Marsh, lying just south of the Dragonmurk.",sec={{t="Heart of the Brood",b="Wyrmbog represents the most heavily infested black dragon territory in southern Kalimdor. Where the open waters of Dustwallow give way to scorched muck and towering bones, whelps and mature drakes patrol the fetid air. The bog is choked with toxic fumes and predatory beasts driven wild by the draconic presence. Travelers foolish enough to wander into these reaches find themselves directly in the shadow of Onyxia's Lair and Emberstrife's cavernous den.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Wyrmbog?",a="Wyrmbog is the treacherous southern region of Dustwallow Marsh, situated south of the Dragonmurk. It is heavily infested with members of the black dragonflight.",al={"wyrmbog","what is wyrmbog","where is wyrmbog"}},{q="Which dragons dwell in Wyrmbog?",a="The black dragonflight commands the territory. Numerous black dragonkin, drakes, and whelps patrol the marsh, while elder wyrms like Emberstrife and the broodmother Onyxia keep their lairs along its southern perimeter.",al={"who lives in wyrmbog","dragons in wyrmbog","what dragons are here"}},{q="Where is Onyxia's Lair located in relation to Wyrmbog?",a="The entrance to Onyxia's Lair is nestled into the rocky spires and cavern openings along the southern edge of the Wyrmbog.",al={"onyxia lair location","where is onyxia","entrance to onyxia"}},{q="Who is Emberstrife?",a="Emberstrife is an ancient black dragon who resides in a cave carved into the rock formations of the Wyrmbog, acting as a powerful guardian within the broodmother's territory.",al={"emberstrife","who is emberstrife","emberstrifes den"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions hunting the black dragonflight, Wyrmbog is the final, treacherous staging ground before reaching Onyxia's threshold.",["faction:Horde"]="Warchief Thrall's scouts keep a wary eye on Wyrmbog, knowing the black dragons nesting so close to the Barrens and Theramore pose a threat to the fragile balance in Kalimdor."},kw={"black dragonflight","dragonmurk","drakes","dustwallow","emberstrife","marsh","onyxia","wyrmbog"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:onyxia-s-lair","subzone:dragonmurk","topic:black-dragonflight","npc:onyxia"},src={"Wyrmbog"}}
E["zone:dustwallow"] = {t="zone",n="Dustwallow Marsh",z="dustwallow",s="Dustwallow Marsh is a vast, sweltering swampland in central Kalimdor, trapped between the arid plains of the Barrens and the Great Sea. Fed by perpetual subterranean springs, its treacherous fens harbor dangerous predators, covert faction skirmishes, and the lurking presence of the black dragonflight. It serves as home to the Alliance fortress-island of Theramore in the east and the Horde-allied Stonemaul ogres of Brackenwall Village to the northwest.",h="Dustwallow Marsh is a vast, sweltering swampland in central Kalimdor, trapped between the arid plains of the...",sec={{t="A Drowned Landscape",b="Before the Great Sundering, Dustwallow was a high, grassy plain teeming with herd animals. The cataclysm shattered the valley, causing the water table to rise and drown the earth in endless stagnant pools, mossy shallows, and choking mud. Underground springs ensure the marsh remains perpetually humid and submerged, blanketed in thick fog and infested with crocolisks, raptors, and spiders. Jagged shallows and wandering bogs make travel perilous for any adventurer stepping off the crumbling causeways.",sp=0},{t="Old Hatreds and Uneasy Truces",b="Dustwallow was largely wild until the aftermath of the Third War, when Lady Jaina Proudmoore led human refugees across the sea to establish the citadel of Theramore Isle on its eastern coast. Soon after, Kul Tiran forces under Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore waged war against Thrall's fledgling Horde, culminating in bloody battles across the wetlands and the Admiral's defeat. Today, an official armistice exists between Theramore and Orgrimmar, yet tension smolders beneath the surface. Theramore struggles with desertions and sabotage, while spies wage quiet, deadly conflicts across the fens.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow of the Wyrmbog",b="The south of the marsh rises into a jagged, rocky quagmire known as the Dragonmurk and the Wyrmbog. Originally settled by the Stonemaul ogres under the Mok'Nathal champion Rexxar, the area became a graveyard when the black dragonflight violently drove the clan from Stonemaul Village. The displaced ogres fled north to Brackenwall Village under Overlord Mok'Morokk, swearing vengeance. Within these jagged crags lurks Onyxia, daughter of Deathwing, directing her brood and weaving sinister machinations far beyond the swamp.",sp=2}},faq={{q="What is the main Alliance settlement here?",a="The Alliance's presence is centered at Theramore Isle, a fortified city-state situated on a rocky island off the eastern coast. Founded by Lady Jaina Proudmoore following the Third War, it connects to Kalimdor by a narrow roadway and maintains vital ship routes to Menethil Harbor in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"alliance base dustwallow","where is theramore","human town dustwallow"}},{q="Where can Horde adventurers find refuge in the swamp?",a="Horde travelers make camp at Brackenwall Village in the northwestern reaches of the marsh. The settlement was founded by the Stonemaul clan of ogres, who joined the Horde under Rexxar and opened their gates to orcish and tauren allies.",al={"horde base dustwallow","where is brackenwall","ogre village"}},{q="Why are there so many black dragons in the southern marsh?",a="The southern region, known as the Wyrmbog and Dragonmurk, is the brood grounds and domain of Onyxia, daughter of Deathwing. Her black dragonspawn violently drove out the Stonemaul ogres and turned the rocky outcroppings and deep caves into nests for whelps and drakes.",al={"wyrmbog dragons","why black dragons here","dragonmurk"},sp=2},{q="What happened to the Stonemaul ogres' original home?",a="The Stonemaul ogres originally dwelt peacefully in Stonemaul Village in the southern marsh. However, the black dragonflight launched a devastating assault, slaughtering many and forcing the survivors to flee northwest to Brackenwall Village.",al={"stonemaul ruins","what happened to stonemaul village","old ogre town"}},{q="Who lives in the lonely cottage out in the Quagmire?",a="The cottage belongs to Tabetha, an eccentric and powerful hermit mage living quietly in the depths of the marsh. Arcane practitioners often seek her out for instruction or assistance with cleansing volatile magical relics.",al={"tabetha's farm","tabetha dustwallow","who is the witch in the swamp"}},{q="What is Alcaz Island and who controls it?",a="Alcaz Island is a heavily guarded isle off the northeast coast of the marsh, held by the Strashaz naga and patrolled by dangerous elite defenders, with hydras lurking in the surrounding waters.",al={"alcaz island","island off coast dustwallow","what is on alcaz"},sp=2}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Dustwallow Marsh hosts Theramore Isle, the heart of the Alliance's presence on Kalimdor. Adventurers arriving via Menethil Harbor guard its causeways while untangling a web of deserters and missing envoys.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde emissaries come to support the beleaguered Stonemaul ogres at Brackenwall Village, repelling dragon incursions from the Wyrmbog and keeping a wary eye on human movements from the coast.",["class:Mage"]="Mages are drawn across the fens to Tabetha's Farm in the Quagmire, seeking out the recluse's unique expertise regarding arcane conduits and ancient power sources."},kw={"alcaz","brackenwall","dustwallow","jaina","marsh","onyxia","quagmire","stonemaul","tabetha","theramore","wyrmbog"},rel={"subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:onyxia-s-lair","subzone:wyrmbog","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","subzone:tabetha-s-farm","quest:1241"},src={"Dustwallow Marsh (Classic)","Dustwallow Marsh"}}
